The Merc with the mouth is heading back  to the Silver Screen and Wolverine is  coming along for the ride but that might  not be the only surprise hiding in Ryan  Reynolds reveal film star Ryan Reynolds  got the internet rumbling Tuesday with  his Sly announcement that Hugh Jackman  would return to the X-Men Universe  opposite Reynolds Deadpool also known as  The Merc with the mouth in Deadpool 3  come 2024 but in the lead up to the big  reveal online one thing is catching  every comic book Fan's eyes in the  teaser for the Deadpool 3 cool there may  also be a major hint at the return of  X-Force Reynolds and Jackman of course  have had a playful rivalry with each  other and their X-Men characters for  years their comedic relationship began  with Reynold's first appearance as Wade  Wilson who would eventually become  Deadpool in the X-Men spin-off movie  X-Men Origins Wolverine in 2009 but  since the film and the slim origin story  of Deadpool weren't very well received  by critics or fans Reynolds among them  the actor worked diligently to to write  the ship ultimately his efforts got a  proper version of Deadpool made in 2016  with Tim Miller in the director's chair  the film was a massive Blockbuster with  nearly 783 million dollars in worldwide  ticket sales it's David Leach directed  sequel Deadpool 2 eclipsed the original  stake with nearly 786 million dollars  globally two years later Reynolds has  definitely amped up the hype for the  long-awaited Deadpool 3 with the Jackman  announcement it's a major coup for the  producer actor considering his friend  and X-Men Ally announced that he would  no longer play Wolverine after the  character's death in Logan and while it  remains to be seen how Reynolds and  Jackman will bring Wolverine into the  MCU another mystery has already been  teased with a small detail in Reynolds  Deadpool 3 announcement video Ryan  Reynolds expertly executed the  announcement of Hugh Jackman returning  to the X-Men Universe by giving a  soul-searching soliloquy which ended  with him asking Jackman whether he  wanted to play Wolverine one more time  Jackman's response fonts was absolutely  perfect yeah sure during the course of  the video Reynolds is shown in various  outfits including casual clothing and  dead times sitting in front of a  typewriter hilariously typing with one  finger wearing a gray jumpsuit Reynolds  is also seen in the gray suit sitting on  a toilet the sight of the suit prompted  the internet to explode with speculation  Deadpool of course wore his maroon  colored suit in the first two Deadpool  films and it's his go-to outfit in the  comics as well however in his stints as  a member of the X-Force team in Uncanny  X-Force he donned a gray costume with  red X highlights it's a different take  on his classic outfit and definitely  makes a unique statement whether  Reynolds gray jumpsuit and the Wolverine  announcement video turns out to be the  return of X-Force is yet to be seen But  since a modified version of the group  including Domino was introduced in  Deadpool 2 the idea of a reimagined  X-Force appearing in Deadpool 3 is  certainly possible from now on we'll be  known as  X-Force interestingly this isn't the  first mention of Deadpool's gray suit  making a live-action appearance before  the release of the second film rumors  began circulating with the debut of one  of the trailers of Deadpool 2. in that  short announcement it appeared that  Deadpool was done in Gray attire the  idea that the gray look could  potentially be a reveal of X-Force was  quickly debunked though when it was  revealed that the Merc suit was entirely  coated with Ash could Reynold's choice  of suit color be him making good on  Deadpool 2's trailer fake out we'll just  have to see when Deadpool 3 arrives at  theaters on September 6 2024.  foreign  [Music]
 

